LICENCE SCOPE

This section is a statement of intent, not legal advice.

- All SkyrimPlatform2 code written for Skyrim Underground is AGPL-3.0-or-later.
- Any mod or gamemode that uses SkyrimPlatform2 is intended to be AGPL-3.0-or-later.
  That includes scripts and packages written against its API and native modules built
  against its module ABI.
- Plugins made with the Creation Kit (ESP, ESM and ESL files) and SKSE plugins that do
  not use SkyrimPlatform2 are separate works and are not covered.
- Whether a script that only calls an API is a derivative work is legally unsettled.
  The Free Software Foundation's view is that plugins which share function calls and
  data structures with their host form a single combined program.
- The additional permission in LICENSE (combining with Skyrim, SKSE and their
  libraries) covers the code contributed to SkyrimPlatform2. Code from other projects
  keeps its own terms.


THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

SkyrimPlatform2 is built with the components below. vcpkg fetches and builds them
from source at the versions pinned in vcpkg-configuration.json and ports/; ORIGINS.md
lists the exact pins. Each component's own licence applies to its code.

Linked into SkyrimPlatform2.dll (their licence texts ship as THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES in
Data/SkyrimPlatform2/):

- CommonLibSSE-NG (alandtse): GPL-3.0-or-later with a Modding Exception and a
  GPL-3.0 Linking Exception. SKSE plugin interface and game layouts. Combined with
  SkyrimPlatform2 under section 13 of GPL-3.0 and AGPL-3.0.
- spdlog: MIT. Logging.
- fmt: MIT. Text formatting, used by spdlog.

Used to build, not linked into SkyrimPlatform2.dll:

- DirectXTK, DirectXMath: MIT. rapidcsv: BSD-3-Clause. Dependencies of
  CommonLibSSE-NG's own build.
- QuickJS-ng: MIT. JavaScript engine; linked into the script layer (sp2_js), the
  sp2-run harness and the unit tests so far, none of which ships yet.
- nlohmann-json: MIT. JSON parsing (header-only); used by the script layer and tests,
  not yet by the DLL.
- Catch2: BSL-1.0. Unit tests only.
